{"id":"world-07-locations-landmarks-and-dungeons","group":"world","groupLabel":"World & Lore","number":"07","title":"Locations Landmarks and Dungeons","summary":"Catalogues locations by production priority and connects visual identity, narrative purpose and gameplay relevance.","sourceFile":"World and Lore/07 - Locations Landmarks and Dungeons.docx","meta":{"status":"DRAFT","version":"0.15.7","owner":"J. Crow","last_updated":"29/08/2026"},"headings":[{"level":1,"text":"1. Document Purpose"},{"level":1,"text":"2. Fundamental Rule"},{"level":1,"text":"3. Location Classification"},{"level":1,"text":"4. Production Priority"},{"level":3,"text":"VERTICAL SLICE"},{"level":3,"text":"WEBSITE / PITCH"},{"level":3,"text":"FUTURE PRODUCTION"},{"level":3,"text":"LORE ONLY"},{"level":1,"text":"5. Initial Master Register"},{"level":1,"text":"6. Arcane Nation as an Explorable Space"},{"level":3,"text":"Status of the name “Fools”"},{"level":1,"text":"7. Eighth Family Park"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Region"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":3,"text":"Historical Function"},{"level":2,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":2,"text":"Visual"},{"level":2,"text":"Gameplay Relevance"},{"level":1,"text":"8. Zhìbǎo Library"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":3,"text":"Function"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"9. Shadow Bar of Oblivion"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":3,"text":"Region"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative Function"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"10. Masutābukku Dojo"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":3,"text":"Function"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":3,"text":"Priority"},{"level":1,"text":"11. Tower of Major Arcana"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Prison / Landmark / Dungeon"},{"level":2,"text":"History"},{"level":1,"text":"Status"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual Function"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"12. Nightmare Laboratories"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"13. Di Eris & Athena Academy"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Region"},{"level":3,"text":"Historical Association"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Academy / Ruin / Laboratory / Dungeon"},{"level":1,"text":"History"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":1,"text":"Current State"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"14. Masutābukku Castle"},{"level":1,"text":"15. Archangel Nation"},{"level":1,"text":"Cardinal Palace and Abandoned Military Base."},{"level":1,"text":"16. Cardinal Palace"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Government Institution / Historic Landmark"},{"level":3,"text":"Region"},{"level":1,"text":"Function"},{"level":1,"text":"History"},{"level":1,"text":"Current State"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"17. Abandoned Military Base"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"History"},{"level":1,"text":"Narrative Function"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"},{"level":1,"text":"18. Mafia Nation"},{"level":2,"text":"Hive-City"},{"level":1,"text":"The underground hive-city."},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Origin"},{"level":1,"text":"Architectural Consequence"},{"level":1,"text":"Social Verticality"},{"level":1,"text":"Pending Internal Locations"},{"level":1,"text":"19. Beast Nation"},{"level":1,"text":"Beast geography remains open."},{"level":2,"text":"Places We Know We Will Need"},{"level":3,"text":"Royal Capital"},{"level":3,"text":"Royal Palace/Residence"},{"level":3,"text":"Grand Academy"},{"level":3,"text":"Kitsune Sanctuaries"},{"level":3,"text":"Research Centers"},{"level":3,"text":"Historical Elemental Edge Temples"},{"level":1,"text":"Tree of Wisdom"},{"level":1,"text":"20. Kingless Island"},{"level":2,"text":"Identity"},{"level":3,"text":"Type"},{"level":1,"text":"Territory / Settlement Network / Historical Landscape"},{"level":1,"text":"History"},{"level":1,"text":"Current State"},{"level":1,"text":"Visual"},{"level":1,"text":"Gameplay"}],"blocks":[{"type":"title","text":"Locations, Landmarks & Dungeons"},{"type":"p","text":"Catalog of Narratively Important Locations"},{"type":"p","text":"Public project: Symphony of Justice | Internal/original name: Symphonia Iustitiae"},{"type":"table","table":0},{"type":"h1","text":"1. Document Purpose"},{"type":"p","text":"Define the locations in Symphony of Justice that need to be recognizable for:"},{"type":"p","text":"narrative;"},{"type":"p","text":"exploration;"},{"type":"p","text":"Level Design;"},{"type":"p","text":"Environment Concept Art;"},{"type":"p","text":"combat;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"Bosses;"},{"type":"p","text":"Vertical Slice;"},{"type":"p","text":"An important location should answer four questions:"},{"type":"p","text":"What is it?\nWhy does it exist?\nWhat happened there?\nWhy should the player remember it?"},{"type":"p","text":"The objective is not to record every house, shop, or cave in the world. This document should focus on places that possess:"},{"type":"p","text":"identity;"},{"type":"p","text":"function;"},{"type":"p","text":"history;"},{"type":"p","text":"visual value;"},{"type":"p","text":"gameplay relevance."},{"type":"h1","text":"2. Fundamental Rule"},{"type":"p","text":"A location should not exist solely because: “we need a Dungeon here.”"},{"type":"p","text":"It must first exist within the world."},{"type":"p","text":"The ideal relationship will be: HISTORY → FUNCTION → ARCHITECTURE → CURRENT STATE → GAMEPLAY"},{"type":"p","text":"That is much stronger than building an abandoned school simply because we want an unsettling setting."},{"type":"h1","text":"3. Location Classification"},{"type":"p","text":"Each place should be identified by a primary category."},{"type":"table","table":1},{"type":"p","text":"A location may belong to multiple categories."},{"type":"h1","text":"4. Production Priority"},{"type":"p","text":"In addition to its canon status, each place will have an independent priority."},{"type":"h3","text":"VERTICAL SLICE"},{"type":"p","text":"Must exist or be defined for the demo."},{"type":"h3","text":"WEBSITE / PITCH"},{"type":"p","text":"Needs Concept Art because it helps sell the universe visually."},{"type":"h3","text":"FUTURE PRODUCTION"},{"type":"p","text":"Important for the full game, but not immediately."},{"type":"h3","text":"LORE ONLY"},{"type":"p","text":"Necessary for historical coherence even if the player may never visit it."},{"type":"h1","text":"5. Initial Master Register"},{"type":"table","table":2},{"type":"h1","text":"6. Arcane Nation as an Explorable Space"},{"type":"p","text":"Historical documentation develops the Arcane region more than any other in terms of specific locations. Arcane Company New Story presents a central area historically called the Village of Fools, composed of spaces associated with different Arcane families."},{"type":"p","text":"However:"},{"type":"h3","text":"Status of the name “Fools”"},{"type":"p","text":"I do not yet think we should declare Fools the definitive name of the capital or central city. It can be retained as:"},{"type":"p","text":"historical name;"},{"type":"p","text":"district;"},{"type":"p","text":"working name;"},{"type":"p","text":"definitive name if you confirm it later."},{"type":"h1","text":"7. Eighth Family Park"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Region"},{"type":"p","text":"Arcane Nation."},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Landmark / Urban Hub."},{"type":"h3","text":"Historical Function"},{"type":"p","text":"It represents the central point where the areas corresponding to the major families converge. The historical source describes it precisely as a central space connecting the seven main zones and serving as a point of balance for the Eighth Family."},{"type":"h2","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"The Eighth Family is especially important because its members:"},{"type":"p","text":"do not necessarily share blood ties;"},{"type":"p","text":"must be accepted by the leaderships;"},{"type":"p","text":"function as an external element within the Arcane hereditary system."},{"type":"p","text":"For this reason, the park can visually represent: the only space in the Arcane political heart that belongs to people who did not inherit their place."},{"type":"p","text":"This gives it tremendous meaning."},{"type":"h2","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"A large circular or radial space. From it, paths could be visible leading toward:"},{"type":"p","text":"family districts;"},{"type":"p","text":"institutional centers;"},{"type":"p","text":"towers;"},{"type":"p","text":"transport routes."},{"type":"p","text":"Materials:"},{"type":"p","text":"wet stone;"},{"type":"p","text":"iron;"},{"type":"p","text":"copper;"},{"type":"p","text":"controlled vegetation;"},{"type":"p","text":"electric lighting."},{"type":"h2","text":"Gameplay Relevance"},{"type":"p","text":"It can function as:"},{"type":"p","text":"hub;"},{"type":"p","text":"orientation point;"},{"type":"p","text":"quests;"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"access to districts."},{"type":"h1","text":"8. Zhìbǎo Library"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Institution / Archive / Landmark."},{"type":"h3","text":"Function"},{"type":"p","text":"Historical center associated with:"},{"type":"p","text":"knowledge;"},{"type":"p","text":"magic;"},{"type":"p","text":"profession;"},{"type":"p","text":"family archives."},{"type":"p","text":"Older sources describe it as the repository of knowledge of the eight families and suggest that its depth could rival the Tower of Major Arcana."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"It should not simply look like a large Victorian library. It needs a unique defining feature. It could expand:"},{"type":"p","text":"vertically;"},{"type":"p","text":"underground;"},{"type":"p","text":"through mechanical archives;"},{"type":"p","text":"restricted sections;"},{"type":"p","text":"suspended walkways."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"It may contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"Arcane documents;"},{"type":"p","text":"family history;"},{"type":"p","text":"censored knowledge;"},{"type":"p","text":"magic;"},{"type":"p","text":"legal records."},{"type":"p","text":"Its potentially unknown depth could allow for much older secrets."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"research;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"document searches;"},{"type":"p","text":"restricted areas;"},{"type":"p","text":"vertical exploration."},{"type":"p","text":"An excellent candidate for Environment Concept Art."},{"type":"h1","text":"9. Shadow Bar of Oblivion"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Social Hub / Landmark."},{"type":"h3","text":"Region"},{"type":"p","text":"Arcane. Historical material presents it as a space associated with the Shadow family, gastronomy, mixology, and the Adventurers’ Guild."},{"type":"p","text":"The exact function of the former “Adventurers’ Guild” should be reviewed because modern Game Design may organize quests differently."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative Function"},{"type":"p","text":"This location can serve as an excellent contrast to the cold Arcane image."},{"type":"p","text":"It can show:"},{"type":"p","text":"food;"},{"type":"p","text":"drink;"},{"type":"p","text":"conversations;"},{"type":"p","text":"rumors;"},{"type":"p","text":"inhabitants outside political functions."},{"type":"p","text":"It is important for nations to have places where: people simply live."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"dark wood;"},{"type":"p","text":"copper;"},{"type":"p","text":"warm lighting;"},{"type":"p","text":"fogged glass;"},{"type":"p","text":"subtle machinery;"},{"type":"p","text":"Akkumu bottles;"},{"type":"p","text":"Shadow family details."},{"type":"p","text":"The contrast of a gray, cold exterior with a warm, lively interior could make it memorable."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"NPCs;"},{"type":"p","text":"stories;"},{"type":"p","text":"quests;"},{"type":"p","text":"information;"},{"type":"p","text":"rest;"},{"type":"p","text":"social tutorial."},{"type":"h1","text":"10. Masutābukku Dojo"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Training Institution."},{"type":"h3","text":"Function"},{"type":"p","text":"Training in:"},{"type":"p","text":"techniques;"},{"type":"p","text":"abilities;"},{"type":"p","text":"combat."},{"type":"p","text":"The historical source describes it as a place where the Masutābukku train people and organize competitions."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"It can show that Arcane society does not understand learning solely as formal education."},{"type":"p","text":"There is also: physical discipline and practice."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"It can function as:"},{"type":"p","text":"training;"},{"type":"p","text":"challenges;"},{"type":"p","text":"advanced tutorial;"},{"type":"p","text":"friendly arenas."},{"type":"h3","text":"Priority"},{"type":"h1","text":"11. Tower of Major Arcana"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"h1","text":"Prison / Landmark / Dungeon"},{"type":"p","text":"One of the most visually powerful historical locations."},{"type":"h2","text":"History"},{"type":"p","text":"Older documentation places it away from the town, but large enough to be visible from there."},{"type":"p","text":"It is also associated with:"},{"type":"p","text":"sinners;"},{"type":"p","text":"former leaders;"},{"type":"p","text":"Deadly Sins;"},{"type":"p","text":"relics;"},{"type":"p","text":"chains;"},{"type":"p","text":"trials."},{"type":"h1","text":"Status"},{"type":"p","text":"The tower deserves to be retained. But I would not automatically assume that: “each upper floor literally contains every former leader.”"},{"type":"p","text":"That requires reviewing the current cosmology of:"},{"type":"p","text":"Sins;"},{"type":"p","text":"death;"},{"type":"p","text":"Purgatory;"},{"type":"p","text":"prisons."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual Function"},{"type":"p","text":"It should dominate part of the Arcane skyline. Principle: the nation can physically look toward the place where it imprisons what it considers unforgivable."},{"type":"p","text":"That works extremely well with the philosophy of Judgment."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"extremely tall tower;"},{"type":"p","text":"blackened stone;"},{"type":"p","text":"metal;"},{"type":"p","text":"monumental chains;"},{"type":"p","text":"architecture that narrows or distorts as it rises;"},{"type":"p","text":"exterior electric lighting."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"Perfect for:"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon;"},{"type":"p","text":"challenge;"},{"type":"p","text":"history of the Sins;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"future content."},{"type":"h1","text":"12. Nightmare Laboratories"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Research Facility / Industrial / Secret Areas."},{"type":"p","text":"They exist narratively as spaces associated with:"},{"type":"p","text":"research;"},{"type":"p","text":"experimentation;"},{"type":"p","text":"technology."},{"type":"p","text":"In the ancient story, they are also connected to events in which Deadly Sins are released."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"research;"},{"type":"p","text":"technology;"},{"type":"p","text":"experiments;"},{"type":"p","text":"combat;"},{"type":"p","text":"secrets;"},{"type":"p","text":"electrical puzzles."},{"type":"h1","text":"13. Di Eris & Athena Academy"},{"type":"p","text":"This deserves an especially strong entry."},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Region"},{"type":"p","text":"Arcane."},{"type":"h3","text":"Historical Association"},{"type":"p","text":"Kokkuren."},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"h1","text":"Academy / Ruin / Laboratory / Dungeon"},{"type":"h1","text":"History"},{"type":"p","text":"In the historical documentation, it is accessed through a hidden tunnel beneath a central area with a mirror."},{"type":"p","text":"Inside are found:"},{"type":"p","text":"rusted experiments;"},{"type":"p","text":"records;"},{"type":"p","text":"logs written from different temporal perspectives;"},{"type":"p","text":"old studies related to immortality;"},{"type":"p","text":"information about PLO;"},{"type":"p","text":"Arz. Goetia."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"It has enormous potential because it connects: Arcane → research → Will/magic → time → PLO → Arz. Goetia."},{"type":"p","text":"It can become one of the major places where the player understands: the danger of trying to turn knowledge into dominion over existence."},{"type":"h1","text":"Current State"},{"type":"p","text":"Historically:"},{"type":"p","text":"abandoned;"},{"type":"p","text":"deteriorated;"},{"type":"p","text":"rusted experiments;"},{"type":"p","text":"partially destroyed laboratory."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"Exterior:"},{"type":"p","text":"academic ruins;"},{"type":"p","text":"garden/park;"},{"type":"p","text":"hidden access."},{"type":"p","text":"Interior:"},{"type":"p","text":"ancient Arcane architecture;"},{"type":"p","text":"laboratories;"},{"type":"p","text":"mirrors;"},{"type":"p","text":"machinery;"},{"type":"p","text":"corrosion;"},{"type":"p","text":"residual elemental energy."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"Dungeon;"},{"type":"p","text":"research;"},{"type":"p","text":"puzzles;"},{"type":"p","text":"combat;"},{"type":"p","text":"Boss;"},{"type":"p","text":"environmental narrative."},{"type":"p","text":"It could even be studied in the future as an alternative candidate for a demo, although it does not currently replace the defined Vertical Slice."},{"type":"h1","text":"14. Masutābukku Castle"},{"type":"p","text":"Historically, it appears as a location where a confrontation against King Shadow and Zileus takes place, including labyrinthine puzzles and a battle on the roof. We first need to resolve something: why do the Masutābukku have a castle? And does it fit their modern identity?"},{"type":"p","text":"It could represent:"},{"type":"p","text":"historical headquarters;"},{"type":"p","text":"fortified monastery;"},{"type":"p","text":"archive;"},{"type":"p","text":"training complex."},{"type":"h1","text":"15. Archangel Nation"},{"type":"p","text":"We have fewer developed locations, but two are especially important:"},{"type":"h1","text":"Cardinal Palace and Abandoned Military Base."},{"type":"p","text":"Both are directly connected to one of the strongest historical narrative conflicts in the nation."},{"type":"h1","text":"16. Cardinal Palace"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"h1","text":"Government Institution / Historic Landmark"},{"type":"h3","text":"Region"},{"type":"p","text":"Archangel."},{"type":"h1","text":"Function"},{"type":"p","text":"Center of the Cardinals, associated with:"},{"type":"p","text":"investigation;"},{"type":"p","text":"justice;"},{"type":"p","text":"institutional authority."},{"type":"h1","text":"History"},{"type":"p","text":"Historical documents develop a takeover of the Cardinal Palace in which:"},{"type":"p","text":"rebels occupy the building;"},{"type":"p","text":"hostages are present;"},{"type":"p","text":"Cardinals attempt to negotiate;"},{"type":"p","text":"military forces intervene;"},{"type":"p","text":"tanks and troops attack;"},{"type":"p","text":"the event becomes a public crisis."},{"type":"p","text":"This event also functions as a historical analogy within the Archangel narrative, according to the project’s contemporary direction."},{"type":"h1","text":"Current State"},{"type":"p","text":"It will depend on when the player visits it."},{"type":"p","text":"It could have been:"},{"type":"p","text":"rebuilt;"},{"type":"p","text":"partially restored;"},{"type":"p","text":"converted into a memorial;"},{"type":"p","text":"still functioning."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"Given the new Archangel visual language:"},{"type":"p","text":"colonial/institutional architecture;"},{"type":"p","text":"large plaza;"},{"type":"p","text":"courtyards;"},{"type":"p","text":"corridors;"},{"type":"p","text":"public halls;"},{"type":"p","text":"modern additions;"},{"type":"p","text":"visible scars of reconstruction."},{"type":"p","text":"Very important: it should not look like a European fantasy palace. It must reflect the current Latin American direction."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative"},{"type":"p","text":"It may contain:"},{"type":"p","text":"memorials;"},{"type":"p","text":"archives;"},{"type":"p","text":"official versions;"},{"type":"p","text":"hidden evidence."},{"type":"p","text":"This allows the same building to tell: one public version through its monuments and another version through what is found hidden."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"urban exploration;"},{"type":"p","text":"narrative;"},{"type":"p","text":"investigation;"},{"type":"p","text":"possible historical/vision mission."},{"type":"h1","text":"17. Abandoned Military Base"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Military Facility / Ruin / Investigation Zone."},{"type":"h1","text":"History"},{"type":"p","text":"During the events related to the Cardinal Palace, the group discovers that the supposedly abandoned base still contains:"},{"type":"p","text":"military personnel;"},{"type":"p","text":"prisoners;"},{"type":"p","text":"archives;"},{"type":"p","text":"evidence of criminal acts;"},{"type":"p","text":"belongings of deceased people."},{"type":"h1","text":"Narrative Function"},{"type":"p","text":"It represents one of the places where: the government’s official version begins to collapse in the face of physical evidence."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"aged military structures;"},{"type":"p","text":"vegetation;"},{"type":"p","text":"concrete;"},{"type":"p","text":"storage areas;"},{"type":"p","text":"offices;"},{"type":"p","text":"interrogation rooms;"},{"type":"p","text":"facilities clandestinely repurposed."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"infiltration;"},{"type":"p","text":"investigation;"},{"type":"p","text":"combat;"},{"type":"p","text":"evidence;"},{"type":"p","text":"exploration."},{"type":"h1","text":"18. Mafia Nation"},{"type":"h2","text":"Hive-City"},{"type":"p","text":"Unlike the Arcane, we still do not have many individual buildings. But we do have one of the strongest macro-locations in the project."},{"type":"h1","text":"The underground hive-city."},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"p","text":"Mega Settlement / Underground Region."},{"type":"h1","text":"Origin"},{"type":"p","text":"The Mafia was:"},{"type":"p","text":"defeated;"},{"type":"p","text":"sealed;"},{"type":"p","text":"confined underground."},{"type":"p","text":"For generations, its population continued developing within the limited space. Historical material already describes this underground megacity and the impossibility of expanding normally."},{"type":"h1","text":"Architectural Consequence"},{"type":"p","text":"extreme vertical growth. The city should have:"},{"type":"p","text":"multiple levels;"},{"type":"p","text":"stacked districts;"},{"type":"p","text":"bridges;"},{"type":"p","text":"elevators;"},{"type":"p","text":"walkways;"},{"type":"p","text":"tunnels;"},{"type":"p","text":"structures added on top of others;"},{"type":"p","text":"repurposed infrastructure."},{"type":"h1","text":"Social Verticality"},{"type":"p","text":"Older documentation already associated lower levels with poorer sectors and upper areas with greater influence."},{"type":"h1","text":"Pending Internal Locations"},{"type":"p","text":"We will later need to define:"},{"type":"p","text":"Hat Mafia territory;"},{"type":"p","text":"Pale Moon;"},{"type":"p","text":"Crimson Eyes;"},{"type":"p","text":"Counts;"},{"type":"p","text":"Low Streets;"},{"type":"p","text":"surface access points;"},{"type":"p","text":"main market;"},{"type":"p","text":"water sources;"},{"type":"p","text":"food production;"},{"type":"p","text":"energy zones."},{"type":"h1","text":"19. Beast Nation"},{"type":"p","text":"At present we know its:"},{"type":"p","text":"culture;"},{"type":"p","text":"architecture;"},{"type":"p","text":"government;"},{"type":"p","text":"very well, but we have few names for specific places."},{"type":"p","text":"This means we need to be honest here:"},{"type":"h1","text":"Beast geography remains open."},{"type":"h2","text":"Places We Know We Will Need"},{"type":"h3","text":"Royal Capital"},{"type":"h3","text":"Royal Palace/Residence"},{"type":"h3","text":"Grand Academy"},{"type":"h3","text":"Kitsune Sanctuaries"},{"type":"h3","text":"Research Centers"},{"type":"h3","text":"Historical Elemental Edge Temples"},{"type":"p","text":"There is historical basis for ancient temples/spaces connected to the masters of those techniques."},{"type":"h1","text":"Tree of Wisdom"},{"type":"p","text":"Historical materials treat it as an extremely important treasure linked to the Beasts."},{"type":"p","text":"We still need to define:"},{"type":"p","text":"whether it is literally a tree;"},{"type":"p","text":"location;"},{"type":"p","text":"size;"},{"type":"p","text":"function;"},{"type":"p","text":"relationship with Kitsune."},{"type":"p","text":"If it remains, it has potential as:"},{"type":"p","text":"because it could become one of the most recognizable landmarks in the world."},{"type":"h1","text":"20. Kingless Island"},{"type":"h2","text":"Identity"},{"type":"h3","text":"Type"},{"type":"h1","text":"Territory / Settlement Network / Historical Landscape"},{"type":"h1","text":"History"},{"type":"p","text":"The Island emerged from communities displaced by ancient conflicts that sought to move away from the major wars."},{"type":"p","text":"It also preserves remains of the ancient Kingdom of Judgment and ruins linked to the Deities and Purgatory. Historical documents already describe it as an independent territory where evidence of that ancient era survives."},{"type":"h1","text":"Current State"},{"type":"p","text":"Inhabited."},{"type":"p","text":"Multicultural."},{"type":"p","text":"Independent."},{"type":"h1","text":"Visual"},{"type":"p","text":"We do not yet have a fully finalized direction. Older documentation imagined it as more:"},{"type":"p","text":"tropical;"},{"type":"p","text":"cheerful;"},{"type":"p","text":"social."},{"type":"p","text":"We know it should convey:"},{"type":"p","text":"serenity;"},{"type":"p","text":"freedom;"},{"type":"p","text":"new beginnings;"},{"type":"p","text":"historical layers."},{"type":"h1","text":"Gameplay"},{"type":"p","text":"In the long term:"},{"type":"p","text":"exploration;"},{"type":"p","text":"social;"},{"type":"p","text":"housing;"},{"type":"p","text":"events;"},{"type":"p","text":"dungeons;"},{"type":"p","text":"activities."},{"type":"p","text":"Historical material already proposed weekly Dungeons within the Island. But: it does NOT need to be built in full for the Vertical Slice."}],"tables":[[["Status","DRAFT","Version","0.15.7"],["Owner","J. Crow","Last updated","29/08/2026"]],[["Category","Definition"],["Settlement","Inhabited city, town, or settlement